  "body": "## What changed\n\n`pr-test.yml` is a `workflow_dispatch`-only workflow (inputs: PR number, head SHA the reviewer read) that runs a PR's quick gate plus clippy on the maintainer's self-hosted Linux runner, so a review needs no 10-20 GB local worktree.\n\n- Runs only for a PR whose author has push access (maintainer decision \"Collaborators only\"): the first step checks it through the API and refuses otherwise; other PRs build locally.\n- Job targets its own runner label `camcraft-pr-test` (maintainer decision \"Separate runner/user\"): own OS user, HOME, cargo home and sccache dir, never the cut/release runner of #1413. `CARGO_HOME` and `SCCACHE_DIR` are set under the runner's work dir.\n- Refuses a diff touching `build.rs`, `.github/`, `scripts/`, `Cargo.toml`/`Cargo.lock`, a toolchain file, a `.cargo/` directory at any depth, or `xtask/`; the diff is listed with `--no-renames`.\n- Checks out `refs/pull/<N>/head`, refuses any head but the SHA given, trial-merges main locally, runs `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` and clippy on touched crates. Read-only token, no secrets, no credentials on disk.\n- Actions pinned by commit SHA; artifact retention 7 days.\n- PR-reviewer agent, `review-prs` skill and AGENTS.md describe the same rules; decision file `docs/decisions/1420-pr-test-pipeline.md` records both decisions and what was dropped. PROCESS_VERSION 58.\n\n## Tested\n\n- Workflow YAML parses; the refusal regex run on sample paths refuses `crates/ui/.cargo/config.toml`, `.cargo/config.toml` and `xtask/src/plan.rs`; `git diff --name-only --no-renames` lists the source side of a rename (without the flag it is hidden).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No Actions run was started and no runner was used: the collaborator-permission step, the runner label and the cache directories are unverified on a live runner.\n\nChangelog: none (process/CI)\nFixes #1420\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
